# Written by `lingui extract`, and the reason it must be excluded is the pre-commit hook:
# lefthook runs its commands in parallel, so `prettier . --write` (the `linter` command) and
# `lingui extract --clean` (the `i18n` command) were writing these exact files at the same time,
# with `stage_fixed: true` re-staging whatever prettier touched, and a
# `git diff --quiet -- src/i18n/messages` assertion running immediately after. Whichever process
# finished last decided the outcome, so the hook could reject a clean tree for catalogue drift
# that did not exist. The formatter in lingui.config.ts already emits 2-space JSON with a
# trailing newline, which is what prettier would have produced.
src/i18n/messages/*.json
